WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.240
The school index has eleven Week 13 rows: autonomic and acid-base review; all clinical pathways; all treatment protocols; valvular disease and murmurs; patient autonomy; medication-safety framework; implementation and evaluation; systems-based practice; antiemetics; self-determination and advocacy; and blood-pressure interpretation.
学校索引列出第13周十一项阅读：自主神经与酸碱复习、全部临床流程、全部治疗方案、瓣膜病和杂音、患者自主权、安全给药框架、实施与评价、系统实践、止吐药、自我决定与倡导，以及血压解释。

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:45.720
Nancy Caroline Canadian eighth edition remains the learner-confirmed principal examination text. The weekly map points to Chapter 48 chronic-care assessment and home-health headings, Chapters 34 and 35 for GI and renal/urologic context, and Chapters 18 and 19 for decisions and documentation.
Nancy Caroline 加拿大第八版仍是学员确认的主考试教材。周主题地图指向第48章慢性照护评估与居家护理、第34及35章胃肠和肾脏泌尿背景，以及第18、19章决策与记录。

00:00:45.720 --> 00:01:11.760
All eleven assigned readers now have source-specific English and Chinese explanations, with the identified files and review extent recorded. This is not merely a list of candidate textbooks. Repeated ranges retain previously checked teaching; newly assigned boundaries and the Week Thirteen applications were reviewed separately. Open each reader for the connected explanation, not just its chapter heading.
十一项指定阅读现均有针对来源的中英文讲解，并记录了已识别文件与核对范围，不再只是候选教材清单。重复范围保留此前核实的讲解，新增边界和第十三周应用另作核对。应打开各读本学习连贯解释，而不只看章节标题。

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:41.232
Real differences remain explicit. The CPSC literal pages discuss drains, so the named medication-safety framework is taught alongside them. The identified school cardiovascular book has the named valve chapter, but not the printed page range in the school table. We teach that complete named chapter without claiming the unresolved pages match. Source-specific limits and current practice comparisons remain visible in the bilingual readers.
真实差异仍须明确。CPSC字面页码讨论引流，因此同时讲解点名的用药安全框架。已识别的学校心血管教材包含指定瓣膜病章节，但与学校表格页码不符；我们完整讲解该点名章节，不声称未解决的页码已经匹配。双语读本保留各来源范围及与现行实践的比较。

00:01:41.232 --> 00:01:55.320
For a mechanism chapter, connect the idea to an observable patient finding and name a competing explanation. For a procedure or medication chapter, write the safety check and provider-level boundary beside the concept.
阅读机制章节时，应把概念与可观察的患者发现联系起来，并列出一种替代解释。阅读操作或药物章节时，则把安全核查和执业层级边界写在旁边。

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:09.432
For every assigned page, keep the page locator in your notes and mark what you personally reviewed. A course summary is not evidence that an assigned figure, table, linked video or entire page range has been completed.
每项指定阅读都应在笔记中保留页码定位，并标记自己实际读过的内容。课程摘要不能证明指定图表、链接视频或整段页码范围已经完成。

00:02:09.432 --> 00:02:29.688
The school plan asks you to learn about PEG/NG and urinary devices. That does not authorize you to remove, advance, flush, reconnect or replace one. The current Emergency Medical Assistants Regulation and employer direction define scope; training must also be current and supervised.
学校计划要求学习 PEG/NG 和泌尿器械，但这并不授权拔除、推进、冲洗、重新连接或更换器械。执业范围由现行《Emergency Medical Assistants Regulation》和雇主指示决定；训练也必须有效并受监督。

00:02:29.688 --> 00:02:47.736
The medication framework in a nursing procedure text does not replace BCEHS medication-safety guidance. For nausea, use current E07 and the applicable drug monograph, and stay within the patient’s indication, provider level, education and service direction.
护理操作教材中的给药框架不能替代 BCEHS 用药安全指导。止吐药应依据现行 E07 和相应药物专论，确保符合患者适应证、执业层级、培训和服务指示。

00:02:47.736 --> 00:03:01.512
For a displaced feeding tube, explain why visible displacement does not tell you where the internal end is. Identify the patient findings that increase urgency and the history that should travel with the handover.
对于移位的喂养管，应解释为什么外观移位不能说明内部管端的位置。指出哪些患者表现会提高紧急程度，以及交接时应附带哪些病史。

00:03:01.512 --> 00:03:17.088
For a catheter with low output, connect the observation to hydration, renal and systemic illness without diagnosing from urine appearance. For nausea, consider serious causes before selecting a pathway-based symptom intervention.
对于尿量减少的导尿管，应把观察结果与水合状态、肾脏及全身疾病联系起来，但不能单凭尿液外观诊断。对于恶心，应先考虑严重病因，再选择符合流程的症状干预。
